## Control {{controlId}}: Limit Management of Audit Logging Functionality to a Subset of Privileged Users

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization limits audit logging management within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant to designated security administrators through role-based access control and PIM, managed by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

{{#if roleAssignmentsConfigured}}
**Audit Management Authorization:**
Only the following privileged role holders can manage audit logging functionality:
{{#if assignments}}
{{#each assignments}}
- **{{principalDisplayName}}** — Role: {{roleDefinitionName}} (Scope: {{scope}})
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

Audit logging configuration (retention periods, audit categories, diagnostic settings) is restricted to Security Administrator and Compliance Administrator roles. Standard administrators cannot modify audit configurations.
{{else}}
Privileged role assignments for audit management have not been confirmed.
{{/if}}

{{#if pimConfigured}}
**Just-in-Time Audit Management:**
PIM enforces time-bound access for audit management roles:
{{#if policies}}
{{#each policies}}
- **{{roleDisplayName}}** — Approval required: {{#if approvalRequired}}Yes{{else}}No{{/if}}, MFA required: {{#if mfaRequired}}Yes{{else}}No{{/if}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

Administrators must activate security roles through PIM before modifying audit configurations, creating an approval chain and audit trail for every change to logging settings.
{{else}}
PIM has not been configured. Audit management access relies on static role assignments.
{{/if}}

**Separation of Duties:**
Audit logging management roles are separated from operational administration roles, preventing administrators from disabling audit trails of their own activities.

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine role assignments for audit management, PIM activation logs, separation of duties documentation, and audit configuration change logs.

